WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.522 --> 00:00:15.611
The had a pig's snout and ears.

2
00:00:17.352 --> 00:00:19.553
he ran on two legs like a person.

3
00:00:20.194 --> 00:00:21.575
He swung the rake again.

4
00:00:22.235 --> 00:00:24.817
Wukong blocked the rake with his iron bar.

5
00:00:26.578 --> 00:00:28.640
Then he swung the bar at the pig's feet.

6
00:00:30.617 --> 00:00:31.337
cried the pig.

7
00:00:31.958 --> 00:00:34.760
He fell facedown in the dirt.

8
00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:35.800
jumped back up.

9
00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.802
"You'll wish you hadn't done that!"

10
00:00:39.863 --> 00:00:45.207
Wukong leaped out of the way as the pig's rake slammed down, smashing a boulder.

11
00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:51.631
The two fought, kicking up dust and rocks.

12
00:00:54.713 --> 00:00:56.954
The Tang Monk hid behind his horse.

13
00:00:58.515 --> 00:01:01.886
now!" Wukong swung his iron bar again.

14
00:01:01.906 --> 00:01:04.027
"I am Sun Wukong.

15
00:01:04.848 --> 00:01:07.810
Five hundred years ago, I caused lots of trouble in Heaven.

16
00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:11.712
The Jade Emperor's entire army couldn't stop me!"

17
00:01:13.574 --> 00:01:15.135
heard of you," said the pig.

18
00:01:15.155 --> 00:01:17.857
"But you don't seem so powerful to me!"

19
00:01:18.957 --> 00:01:20.558
lunged at the monkey again.

20
00:01:21.379 --> 00:01:22.900
Wukong jumped out of the way.

21
00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:26.202
"I thought you were being punished," said the pig.

22
00:01:27.183 --> 00:01:28.384
swung his rake again.

23
00:01:29.064 --> 00:01:30.705
"Weren't you trapped under a mountain?"

24
00:01:30.785 --> 00:01:33.667
"I'm free now," said Wukong.

25
00:01:33.687 --> 00:01:38.229
"I'm going to the West with the Tang Monk to—" Tang Monk!"

26
00:01:38.489 --> 00:01:39.230
cried the pig.

27
00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:40.891
He dropped his rake.

28
00:01:42.231 --> 00:01:43.772
"I'm supposed to go with him too!"

29
00:01:43.792 --> 00:01:45.153
"You are?"

30
00:01:45.613 --> 00:01:46.434
asked Wukong.

31
00:01:48.095 --> 00:01:50.996
"I was sent to Earth as a punishment," said the pig.

32
00:01:52.097 --> 00:01:53.378
name is Zhu Bajie.

33
00:01:55.899 --> 00:01:58.852
I caused trouble in Heaven too.

34
00:01:58.932 --> 00:02:02.616
Guanyin said I would be forgiven if I helped protect the Tang Monk."

35
00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:07.440
rubbed his chin.

36
00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.822
"Okay," he said.

37
00:02:09.842 --> 00:02:12.083
"You can carry the bags."

38
00:02:14.506 --> 00:02:18.949
Zhu Bajie joined the group, and the three of them continued west.

39
00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:22.792
As they traveled, the pig kept complaining.

40
00:02:24.394 --> 00:02:26.395
bags are so heavy!

41
00:02:27.488 --> 00:02:29.469
Do we really need to bring them?"

42
00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:32.850
"Stop complaining," snapped Wukong.

43
00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:36.532
"Going to the Western Paradise is to be difficult."

44
00:02:38.513 --> 00:02:39.233
pig moaned.

45
00:02:39.253 --> 00:02:41.294
"I'm hungry too.

46
00:02:42.554 --> 00:02:44.115
When are we going to eat lunch?"

47
00:02:45.015 --> 00:02:46.296
The Tang Monk frowned.

48
00:02:47.276 --> 00:02:48.197
just ate breakfast.

49
00:02:48.997 --> 00:02:50.418
How can you be hungry again?"

50
00:02:51.778 --> 00:02:55.840
They went around a bend and saw a large tiger.

51
00:02:56.868 --> 00:02:59.890
Bajie and Wukong quickly pulled out their weapons.

52
00:03:01.131 --> 00:03:01.531
are you?"

53
00:03:01.991 --> 00:03:02.872
yelled Bajie.

54
00:03:02.892 --> 00:03:04.673
"What are you doing here?"

55
00:03:06.194 --> 00:03:11.497
"My master, the great king Yellow Wind, is hosting a feast," said the tiger.

56
00:03:12.758 --> 00:03:13.978
looked at the Tang Monk.

57
00:03:15.459 --> 00:03:17.400
"I'm gathering people to eat."

58
00:03:18.981 --> 00:03:22.924
The Tang Monk's face turned pale, and he fell off his horse.

59
00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:26.001
"Don't you dare harm our master!"

60
00:03:26.322 --> 00:03:27.202
Bajie warned.

61
00:03:28.303 --> 00:03:29.164
is the Tang Monk.

62
00:03:29.784 --> 00:03:32.106
He's going to the West to get the True Scriptures."

63
00:03:33.407 --> 00:03:35.408
The tiger's eyes opened wide.

64
00:03:35.428 --> 00:03:40.312
"I heard that eating the Tang Monk will make someone live forever."

65
00:03:41.373 --> 00:03:42.934
tiger showed his claws.

66
00:03:44.735 --> 00:03:46.416
Then he lunged at Bajie.

67
00:03:47.497 --> 00:03:49.018
pig hit him with the rake.

68
00:03:49.599 --> 00:03:52.480
The tiger tumbled over.

69
00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:55.002
Wukong ran toward the tiger with his iron bar.

70
00:03:55.883 --> 00:03:59.686
The tiger dodged the bar and then almost got hit by the rake again.

71
00:04:00.446 --> 00:04:01.687
He turned and fled.

72
00:04:03.789 --> 00:04:05.750
and Bajie ran after the tiger.

73
00:04:08.712 --> 00:04:10.133
For a moment they lost him.

74
00:04:11.614 --> 00:04:15.177
Then they spotted a flash of orange behind some bushes.

75
00:04:15.197 --> 00:04:17.319
"There he is!"

76
00:04:17.759 --> 00:04:19.780
whispered Bajie.

77
00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:22.341
The monkey and pig sneaked up to the bushes.

78
00:04:23.502 --> 00:04:24.842
the tiger wasn't there.

79
00:04:25.582 --> 00:04:34.046
Instead a tiger skin lay over a Wukong laughed.

80
00:04:34.066 --> 00:04:37.507
"He was so scared, he ran right out of his skin!"

81
00:04:38.968 --> 00:04:40.488
slapped Bajie on the back.

82
00:04:40.508 --> 00:04:43.069
"We are great protectors!"

83
00:04:46.011 --> 00:04:48.752
The two friends walked back to the road, laughing.

84
00:04:50.765 --> 00:04:52.947
But suddenly their laughter stopped.

85
00:04:54.228 --> 00:04:54.748
"Oh no!"

86
00:04:55.049 --> 00:04:55.889
cried Wukong.

87
00:04:55.909 --> 00:04:58.311
"Where is the Tang Monk?"
